  "verbalization": "Alitretinoin, a retinoid derivative, is consistently linked to Panel leukemia (Carcinoma cell lines) through its interaction with a common target molecule, 3-[2-[4-[5-[2-(2,3-Dihydroxyphenyl)ethyl]-2-hydroxyphenoxy]phenyl]ethyl]benzene-1,2-diol. This compound is identified as a target of alitretinoin in multiple pathways, with evidence from three distinct datasets showing that alitretinoin inhibits this molecule in various carcinoma cell lines. The shared mechanism of action across these pathways suggests a potential role for alitretinoin in targeting a common molecular pathway involved in leukemia progression. The evidence is supported by a consistent target relationship, with the same target molecule being implicated in multiple cell line models of Panel leukemia. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that alitretinoin may exert its anti-leukemic effects through the inhibition of this specific target, potentially influencing key cellular processes in leukemia cells.",
